OL,3,A'The music transported us to another
OL,4,Aplanet'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Vivienne Dawes first saw the
OL,7,Fphotograph of herself dancing on a
OL,8,Fcrowded dance floor almost 50 years
OL,9,Fago, it felt like being transported
OL,10,Fback in time.
OL,12,FCaptured at Wolverhampton's Culture
OL,13,FCentre in 1978, the image shows her
OL,14,Famong a group of young people immersed
OL,15,Fin a night of music and dancing.
OL,17,FAt the time, none of them could have
OL,18,Fknown the photograph would become an
OL,19,Ficonic image that has been viewed
OL,20,Facross the world and one of
OL,21,Fphotographer Chris Steele-Perkins' most
OL,22,Frecognised works.
OL,23,APub: 04-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,169,160,200,105,0,100
